    "hypothesis": "GeoDAWN Area 2 was flown at 400 m line spacing / 150-200 m drape, so the provided-band geophysical crests (edge_scarp_pot) locate the fault fabric only to ~1 kernel radius. Moving 20% of R1's dots from the coldest to the hottest 5 km prior blocks re-allocates fixed mass onto the crests the blind off-catalogue SGMC control already favours, and should raise live DTI.",
    "mechanism": "Within the 3 px triangular kernel a dot keeps credit 1 - d/3. Mass welded to a surviving host in a high edge_scarp_pot block sits closer to the geophysical offset that the blind control rewards; the move consumes no extra mass (count fixed at 37,654) and every receiver stays >3 px from the mapped catalogue.",
    "non_fault_mimic": "edge_scarp_pot maxima also follow welded-tuff caprock breaks, Lake Lahontan shorelines and 400 m aeromagnetic flight-line corrugation; concentrating on them can cluster dots onto a non-fault gradient with no new-fault truth.",
    "confounder": "Concentration raises block-density CV away from the reported 0.51-0.59 sweet spot and away from the repeated 'spacing/uniformity is the lever' result. The label-free w-field MODEL rewards densification while blind SGMC has preferred spacing in every session; the two instruments are expected to disagree, so no arm is promoted on an instrument and a live |delta| < 0.01 is no evidence.",
    "predicted_sign_size": "Near-zero, sign-uncertain (preregistered point |delta| <= 0.002, range spans zero). A >= +0.01 live gain on the actually-submitted R1 anchors the concentration direction; <= -0.01 closes it and confirms the uniformity lever.",
    "falsifier": "A live receipt <= R1 - 0.01 while both 1 km doses are also negative falsifies crest-concentration on the gate-clean parent; a win of the 5 km arm over the 1 km arm at matched 20% arbitrates the spatial scale of the prior.",
    "preregistration": "registry/preregistration_concentration_r1.json",
